@prefix sh:      <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix sosa:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .
@prefix sensing: <http://example.org/orexis/sensing#> .

#################  How badly an observation-backed want is unmet  #################
#
#  SENSING'S, whole (a-desire-states-its-own-measure, completed by the extraction): the core
#  is BDI, so the kernel derives the want, its met-shape and its node — the mind's structure —
#  and how badness is MEASURED is planning-domain machinery, a capability's contribution. A
#  want about an observed property is measured by a reading against the aim, and the reading
#  is this capability's whole subject; the choir's `urgency` hook has always listed what
#  modules contribute, and this is that instinct made a declaration.
#
#  READ BY THIS PACKAGE'S OWN CODE (`module.py`), never by a kernel loader: the kernel asks
#  "how urgent is this desire, in this world" through `Module.desire_urgency` and holds no
#  measure vocabulary, no measure graph, no evaluator. Which is why the words here are
#  sensing's own — `sensing:measureOf`, not `orexis:` — the repo's promotion test being a word
#  SEVERAL packages must speak, and today one does. When the market ships its duty measure by
#  this same mechanic, promotion happens then.
#
#  ONE declaration for the KIND, not a text per desire: `sensing:measureOf
#  sosa:ObservableProperty` says "a want about an observable property is measured by this
#  SELECT", and the module answers for a desire by asking the store what its
#  `ssn:forProperty` object IS. Nothing is compiled anywhere: the aim is read out of $beliefs
#  by the query itself, and the region's numbers arrive as substituted parameters read off
#  the deduced shapes at answer time — so a re-pick or a re-derivation moves the answer with
#  no text rebuilt.
#
#  The contract: one binding, ?urgency in 0..1. Zero exactly at the aim ($centre stands in
#  while no aim is picked — where an agent with no other reason to prefer would aim), rising
#  with distance scaled by the survival room on the side the value sits ($outerLow below,
#  $outerHigh above — the survival bound where the world states one, the region's own edge
#  where it does not). The asymmetry is deliberate and old: how bad it is to be 0.05 out
#  depends on how much room there is in that direction.

#  TWO declarations now, and they resolve by different roads because they are measures of
#  different KINDS of thing. A region want is about a PROPERTY, and what that property is is a
#  fact the world holds, so `sosa:ObservableProperty` is asked of whichever world is being
#  judged. A freshness want is about KNOWING, and no world holds a type for that: the want
#  names the INSTRUMENT it was derived from, and a want that names one is a want about
#  knowing, by construction rather than by a flag. One file, one word, one evaluator.
#
#  `sensing:Freshness` is a class this package's `desires.ru` puts on every such want, so a
#  sovereign reading the desire modality sees what kind of thing it is holding and this
#  declaration has something to be the measure OF. Nothing dispatches on it — the module reads
#  the instrument the kernel hands over — which is why the type and the behaviour cannot drift
#  apart into two answers.

sensing:FreshnessMeasure
    sensing:measureOf sensing:Freshness ;
    rdfs:label "whether what I know about this instrument is still about now" ;
    rdfs:comment "Evaluated against whichever world is being judged, exactly as the aim measure is — and the measure never names it (#666): the door is handed the world, $instruments the graph holding the horizons this agent has published, and $sensor the instrument this want is about. A look reaches 0.0 in the world it would make, which is what lets the search prefer looking over standing still. $sensor rather than $instrument, because a parameter that is a PREFIX of another is substituted into the middle of it — measured, as `GRAPH <…sensor>s {`, which the parser reports as a missing brace fifty characters away." ;

    #  BINARY, and the gradient it does not have is the interesting part. Age-against-horizon
    #  is the natural continuous measure and this deliberately is not it: a graded freshness
    #  urgency is nonzero the moment a reading is a second old, and a look always reaches 0.0,
    #  so every deliberation tick would find looking an improvement and ask for a reading —
    #  the board woken on the agent's patience clock rather than on its cadence, for ever. The
    #  deadband a region want gets for free (`dose_for` sizes to ~0 near the aim, so the effect
    #  predicts no change and the candidate is pruned) has no analogue here, because a look
    #  always fully refreshes whatever it is worth. What would supply one is the PRICE of
    #  looking, which this package's seams have wanted since v1 and nothing yet charges: with a
    #  cost to weigh, a gradient becomes rankable against it and this measure can grow one.
    #  Until then the honest statement is the one the horizon already makes — inside it the
    #  reading is evidence, outside it is not.
    #
    #  THE FINAL COALESCE IS THE WHOLE ERROR STORY, and it is load-bearing three times over.
    #  An unbound `?at` (nothing ever read this), an unbound `?horizon` (no rhythm published
    #  for this sensor yet) and any arithmetic that raises all make the comparison error, and
    #  an errored expression leaves its variable unbound while keeping the row — so without
    #  this the column would read empty and every ranking caller would have had to guess. It
    #  lands on 1.0: not knowing is maximal, as it is everywhere here, and — the half that
    #  matters most (#342) — a missing horizon reads as maximally urgent rather than as
    #  perfectly fresh. The met-shape beside it fails the same way round for the same reason.
    sh:select """
        SELECT ?urgency WHERE {
            OPTIONAL { 
                ?obs sosa:hasFeatureOfInterest $subject ;
                     sosa:observedProperty $property ;
                     #  Made by MY instrument, matching the met-shape clause for clause. Both
                     #  halves have to carry it or the search finds by satisficing what the
                     #  met-test refuses: a dose's predicted reading would score this want at
                     #  0.0 and buying would look like a way to find something out.
                     sosa:madeBySensor $sensor .
                     #  AND STILL EVIDENCE, which is a FACT and no longer arithmetic (#598).
                     #  This asked `?at + horizon > NOW()`, of every candidate world, against
                     #  the horizon the instruments graph carries — the real clock, inside a
                     #  search, about a world nobody is in. Sensing writes `staleSince` when
                     #  the horizon runs out and the reading it was written on goes with the
                     #  node at the next upsert, so a look's predicted reading is evidence
                     #  by construction and the one it replaced is not there to ask about.
                     FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?obs sensing:staleSince ?since }  }
            #  UNBOUND IS MAXIMAL, which is the whole error story and load-bearing twice:
            #  nothing ever read this pair, or everything it read has gone cold. Both land on
            #  1.0 — not knowing is maximal, as it is everywhere here (#342) — and a sensor
            #  whose horizon this agent cannot state has its reading marked cold on arrival,
            #  so that half of #342 is kept where it can be seen rather than in a COALESCE.
            BIND(IF(BOUND(?obs), 0.0, 1.0) AS ?urgency)
        }""" .

sensing:AimDistanceMeasure
    sensing:measureOf sosa:ObservableProperty ;
    rdfs:label "distance from the aim, scaled by the survival room on that side" ;
    rdfs:comment "Evaluated against whichever world is being judged: the belief base for the live number, a candidate possible world inside the planner — and the measure names neither (#666), the door is told which. $value is a caller-supplied number to judge — the choir asks about readings not yet written, and about predicted ones — or the live reading when the caller supplies none." ;
    #  ?distance <= 0 answers FIRST and without dividing, and that ordering is an engine fact,
    #  not style: pyoxigraph 0.5.9 binds NOTHING for `0.0 / 0.3` — a zero dividend fails the
    #  decimal division a nonzero one survives — so an agent exactly at its aim would read as
    #  maximally urgent through the COALESCE below. Measured, and pinned in
    #  tests/test_desires.py beside the duration limit it rhymes with. The final COALESCE is
    #  the other half of the same discipline: an unmeasured property, and any arithmetic
    #  error, land on 1.0 explicitly — not knowing is maximal, as it is everywhere.
    sh:select """
        SELECT ?urgency WHERE {
            OPTIONAL { 
                ?obs sosa:hasFeatureOfInterest $subject ;
                     sosa:observedProperty $property .
                #  The bands INSIDE the reading's own pattern: outside it, an unbound ?obs
                #  would join freely with any reading of any property in any band. THREE, by
                #  the sovereign's ruling: outside the region is outside it, whichever way,
                #  and how much worse a dying reading is than an uncomfortable one is said by
                #  the survival room the numeric branch above scales by — asked where a number
                #  is in hand, which is where the difference can be seen.
                OPTIONAL { ?obs a sensing:BelowRegion . BIND(0.75 AS ?u3) }
                OPTIONAL { ?obs a sensing:AboveRegion . BIND(0.75 AS ?u4) }
                OPTIONAL { ?obs a sensing:InRegion . BIND(0.0 AS ?u5) }  }
            OPTIONAL { GRAPH $beliefs {
                $me sensing:aims ?aim .
                ?aim ssn:forProperty $property ;
                     schema:value ?picked } }
            #  THE NUMBER ONLY WHERE A CALLER HANDS ONE IN (#579): a world is judged by the
            #  band its reading is in, the one the agent stands in and one a rule imagined
            #  alike, so the two are on one scale; the reading's own number is not read here.
            BIND($value AS ?v)
            BIND(COALESCE(?picked, $centre) AS ?target)
            BIND(IF(?v < ?target, ?target - $outerLow, $outerHigh - ?target) AS ?room)
            BIND(IF(?v < ?target, ?target - ?v, ?v - ?target) AS ?distance)
            #  BY THE BAND where the reading has no number (#579): a reading an effect
            #  predicted is what it IS and nothing more, and this package says how urgent each
            #  band is — outside the region three quarters, inside it nothing. Coarser than the
            #  distance, which is the ruling's point: a pot at 25 and a pot at 27 are one world.
            #  The number, where there is one, still says how far.
            BIND(COALESCE(IF(?distance <= 0, 0.0, IF(?room <= 0, 1.0,
                 IF(?distance / ?room < 1.0, ?distance / ?room, 1.0))),
                 ?u3, ?u4, ?u5, 1.0) AS ?urgency)
        }""" .
